-- Experiment 182 -- SIAM 100-Digit Challenge, Appendix D Problem 7 (FriCAS column).
-- The 1-D statement (region_area.m) needs the island ends y1, y2, y3 and the
-- kink yc as roots of transcendental equations (g(y) = 1, -log g(y) = y^2).
-- FriCAS has no built-in numeric root finder for a non-polynomial equation
-- (solve/realSolve are polynomial-only), so both rows are SKIP rather than a
-- hand-written Newton iteration.  Its quadrature (romberg) would otherwise
-- state the integrals.
)read ../siam100_common.input )quiet
vskip("d7.machine", "FindRoot")
vskip("d7.wp50", "FindRoot")
)quit
